    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2c942844_906db188",
        "filename": "sdk/update.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 303,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-28T23:23:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m worried about properties like this.  If I understand this correctly, Soong from one branch is going to generate an Android.bp file that will be checked in to another branch, but we make no guarantee that the syntax or semantics of properties will be identical across branches.  Would it be better to write out some sort of descriptor as JSON or protobuf, and then have an importer in the receiving branch that can convert it into whatever the local branches Android.bp format is?  That way you can regenerate all of these from their descriptors if the properties need to change, or you can regenerate an old descriptor with a fix and import it into a new branch.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 302,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 303,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "fc9619e92b558cab4aaa28e0027b66361c91bda1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a462ef2_37853967",
        "filename": "sdk/update.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 303,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-29T03:28:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I in general agree with you, but I want to introduce the intermediate format after we really introduce such a breaking change. Making the importer, maintaining it, running it every time we update an SDK all will be a quite burden to me and others, especially given that everything is one the same branch (at least in R).",
      "parentUuid": "2c942844_906db188",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 302,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 303,
        "endChar": 40
      },
